<!DOCTYPE html><html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
<head>
  <title>Insoldia: Program for computing the solar radiation during one
  day</title>
<meta content="text/html; charset=ISO-8859-1" http-equiv="Content-Type"/></head>

<body>
  <!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent al títol de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<h1><span id="wpstitol"/></h1>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent títol de la MSA editable de el WPS.-->
<!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<span id="wpsopcions"/>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA editable de el WPS.-->

  <p>The diffuse radiation is estimated from the direct radiaton and the
  exoatmospheric direct solar irradiance is estimated with the Page equation
  (1986) and fitted by Baldasano et. al. with information from Catalonia
  1994.</p>

  <p>It is necessary to provide the solar exoatmospheric irradiance for the
  wavelength you want, in W/(m2 · micrometer), the tau extinction constant and
  the shadows files in one hour intervals (OMBRESDIA.BAT). If you wish to do
  the calculation for the whole solar spectrum, you must introduce the value
  of 1367 W/m2 as exoatmospheric irradiance, and the value of 0.288 as tau
  (clear forest medium atmosphere, Rothermel 1986).</p>

  <p>The solar position is calculated for the centre of the DEM. The result of
  the program is a file in 10 KJ/(m2 · micrometer) (2 bytes/pixels). The DEM
  (2 bytes/pixels), the lighting matrix (1 byte/pixel) and the temporary
  radiation calculation matrix (4 bytes/pixels) are loaded in the memory.</p>

  <p>Papers that shows and discuss used algorithm:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <p>PONS, X. (1996) <a href="http://magno.uab.cat/atles-climatic/catala/rad_pot.htm">&quot;Solar
      radiation estimation from digital elevation models. Methodological
      proposal&quot;</a> in Juaristi, J &amp; I. Mor. &quot;Geographic
      Information Models and Systems&quot; (458 p) p. 87-97 ISBN:
      84-605-5896-7.</p>
    </li>

    <li>PONS, X. and NINYEROLA, M. (2008) <a href="http://www3.interscience.wiley.com/cgi-bin/fulltext/117934993/PDFSTART">
      &quot;Mapping a topographic global solar radiation model implemented in
      a GIS and refined with ground data&quot;</a> in International Journal of
      Climatology (DOI: 10.1002/joc.1676).
    </li>
  </ul>
  <hr/>

